{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree","id":1384979,"title":"The demon tree","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T18:58:04-07:00","id":1384979,"title":"The demon tree","content":"Apologies if I had already posted this. <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Demon Tree's origin was one that was unknown. Appearing during a wyld storm, it appeared in a deserted homestead of a poor farmer. So poor was the land, that no one bothered to tax it. The land was poor enough that its inhabitants were often starving.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">One day, the man wept, the harvest having failed once again for the 3rd time. There, he laid against the tree, staring up at its bare branches. He wondered if he would have to watch his daughter die. And then, a voice, came from the tree. It was like tinkling bells and the soft whisper of a bubbling brook. It was the sound of rustling grass, and the fall of snow. It sounded, like music. And it whispered, that for the price of blood, it shall bear fruit, that shall save the harvest.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The man cut his palms on an iron knife, and let the blood drip onto the soil at the tree's base. And then, a miracle happened. The tree stirred, and lowered several of its branches. And those branches bloomed with fruit. The farmer took the fruit, burying them in the lands of his farm. The next day, his crops grew to full height. News spread, and soon farmers from around the land came to the tree, offering up the blood of their bodies, their families, and their animals. And the tree began to bloom, soft pink petals growing from once bare branches.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The tree then spoke once again. &quot;Bring me your cattle, such that I may reward you for them.&quot; The first to die was a horse, half-blind and not strong enough to carry a man. It died, and as its body rotted, the tree grew fruit once more, fruits similar to grapes. &quot;Give it to your cattle, that they may grow strong.&quot; And they did, and the animals grew strong and fat, with many litters and many offspring. They grew tall and strong, and they gave good milk and good wool and pulled great loads, and they only needed the barest of care. The people who ate the fruits, grew strong and healthy, and even the elderly could walk and run, and the sickly and lame could stand tall. The fruits and animals plowed the land, and the farming community, once constantly on the brink of starvation, grew prosperous. And men came to the tree, and gave offerings. And the tiny, starving hamlet grew to a booming town, as more children lived, and fewer elderly died.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Years passed, and the tree then spoke, once more. &quot;Grant me a human, such that I may give you gifts.&quot; And many baulked at that. For human sacrifice was banned. But others condemned them, saying that since the tree had given them so much, saving their lives and granting them prosperity. Surely, it was worthy? Besides, it had given them so much, things which they could have never dreamed of. And there was a great argument. Those who condemned the tree were branded as heretics to the great Sakura. And those that argued against human sacrifice were taken, and slain. And the tree was pleased. And for each man slain, a great fruit grew from the branch, and it was split open.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And what treasures were contained inside! One contained a bolt of cloth. A man saw it, and swore it was like silk, only more beautiful. It was cut, and turned into a robe for the priest of the Tree. There was one where instead of seeds, there were jewels embedded within the flesh. One cracked open like an egg, and a great bird of paradise flew out, a sweet song from its beak. Another contained a knife, beautiful and elegant, its blade and hilt of the same material, shining in the light.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">At the sight of these things men grew greedy. Once their community espoused the virtues of hardwork, loyalty, diligence, and determination. And at the sight of the treasures, their hearts grew black. The first to go were the criminals. Thieves, murderers, and bandits. Any who sought to steal their cattle or rob their granaries, were offered to the tree as sacrificed. And when that wasn't enough, they sought to find travellers, waylay them on their journey, and accuse them as bandits, so as to use their souls as currency. And when there were no more travellers and no more criminals, they turned on each other, each and every sacrifice requiring a smaller crime to be punished, until the only ones left were those who bowed to the priest of the Tree.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Years passed</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The village is gone now, and in its place is a giant city, roaring with pride and the strength of civilisation. Guild caravans enter, bringing in tides of slaves, and exit with piles of treasure. The lands surrounding it are fertile and well-watered, and great herds of sheep and cows wander the meadows. A great army had been raised from the farmers who once lived there, guarding the territory and the walls of the city. King and Queens come for the fruit, seeking the longevity its fruit would grant them. Legions of mercenaries are hired using the treasures of the Sakura Tree, enhanced by its fruit. The city is mighty, bearing on the</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">As for the tree? It was once a barren tree, sitting out on the wasteland. Then, it was attended by priests, offerings laid at its trunk. And now, it is at the central courtyard of the palace, attended by a thousand of the most loyal warriors, access to it granted only to the most loyal of servants. And its branches? Where it was once bare, there is now a glorious crown of pink petals, shining even in the night.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A/N: Some say that the pink colour of Sakura petals were due to corpses buried beneath them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">For the purpose of this setting part, everyone wants the tree. Everyone. Even the ones who decry the use of human sacrifice still want to use it because the health benefits are so immense. Adventurers can be rebels, taken as slaves, rulers trying to stop the usage of sacrifice, or even unlucky saps waylaid and accused as bandits.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:00:00-07:00","id":1385002,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, I like also how this story like many good Exalted seeds is described in a pretty setting agnostic fashion, with only really the mention of Wyldstorms to link it to a specific gameline.<br /> <br /> I had a demon tree in my game. It was the Trepletre which mortals may have confused as the Treple Tree or Triple Tree and that may be partially responsible for its appearance as a grand triangular tree which may appear like a great conifer but upon closer inspection it timber is closer to that of some sort of otherworldly oak. If you carved your name onto it you could climb its steps and enter its treehouse layer. It could serve as a sorcerous tutor appearing in the dreams of those who carved their names upon its wood and instructing them through words bled through its walls.<br /> <br /> It also had fruit that tasted sweet and overly ripe, these were as much eggs as seed bearing fruit and when eaten the wyrm riddled flesh could infest mortal souls granting them demonic boons which start subtle but become very obvious if you indulge in the fruit beyond the initial first sampling. In my game a dying village found it and they took up the tradition of having the town leader flay their skin and bury it under the trees roots becoming that Generations Skinless Man, a demonic being who can enter dreams and is attended by the Skinmen the ghosts of past Skinless Men who inhabit their own hides. The town was dying because of famine and seeming infertility, but they discovered that if you ate the fruit and coupled in a primal ritual you could conceive, they didn't realize that the children born from such couplings lacked a mortal soul and in its place lived the maggots of the wyrmridden fruit. In the games prologue for one of the Players the latest Skinless Man started an initiative to grow the town into a city by having animals couple with demons, and trade with Hell so they could grow Tinferns and Brass Bamboo to harvest for supplies and trade, and Bonefruit (which can be ground into meal), and Meatfruit. This combined with the milk from the demonic cattle made them a breadbasket region. By the time they got back to it was a growing boomtown, and most of farm animals had curled horns, including the rabbits and chooks (lil dinosaur chickens native to the area).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:25:40-07:00","id":1385008,"title":"","content":"We need better setting hooks then trees. <br /> <br /> Maybe caves or lakes instead? <br /> <br /> Or an abandoned house?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:53:10-07:00","id":1385204,"title":"","content":"Or Haunted Card Games!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:13:16-07:00","id":1385217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1385204#post1385204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Haunted Card Games!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yu Gi Oh? <br /> <br /> What, something made by Plentimon for gambling, letting you bet anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:33:25-07:00","id":1385219,"title":"","content":"This is a good idea.<br /> <br /> But I'm unclear on how a backwards village which sacrifices anyone who isn't part of its cult, and abandons the virtues of &quot;hardwork, loyalty, diligence, and determination&quot; suddenly becomes a city?<br /> <br /> Step 1: Murderously butcher our townsmen until only the priest and their sycophants survive<br /> Step 2: ???<br /> Step 3: Be a bustling metropolis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:41:47-07:00","id":1385222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1385219#post1385219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good idea.<br /> <br /> But I'm unclear on how a backwards village which sacrifices anyone who isn't part of its cult, and abandons the virtues of &quot;hardwork, loyalty, diligence, and determination&quot; suddenly becomes a city?<br /> <br /> Step 1: Murderously butcher our townsmen until only the priest and their sycophants survive<br /> Step 2: ???<br /> Step 3: Be a bustling metropolis</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me think for a moment...<br /> <br /> Ok, first of all, the fields and farms? They're better now. Now they're even more fertile than most other lands. That's a reason for people to go there. And then there's the guild caravans that go there in search for the precious stuff the demon tree gives out. So then that's a source of trade. I mean sure, the abandonment of the values shit was mostly rhetoric. Its basically the old value systems are now thrown away in favor of greed and cruelty and human sacrifice. Then they took the money and then started buying equipment, tools to work the land, etc.... having a good trade surplus of not only luxuries like tea or vases or cloth, but also in things like 'has a stable food supply so we're able to live for years in a famine'. That tends to attract people. <br /> <br /> People wandered in, growing, and they were accepted as long as they swore oaths to the demon tree. The rate of murder versus the rate of people coming in balanced out when the head priests realized that without anyone to defend them, they'll die to the next fair folk incursion or beastmen raid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T04:20:03-07:00","id":1389933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1385217#post1385217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yu Gi Oh?<br /> <br /> What, something made by Plentimon for gambling, letting you bet anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a Supernal game that 3rd Circle souls played, and Mortals draw upon an echo of it that acts as both a Tarot and a cardboard game like FF8's Triple Triad, which I totally borrow for my games.<br /> <br /> Or a Deva or 3rd Circle Soul that exists as a haunted Game, like a Memetic entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T05:23:23-07:00","id":1389936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1389933#post1389933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe a Supernal game that 3rd Circle souls played, and Mortals draw upon an echo of it that acts as both a Tarot and a cardboard game like FF8's Triple Triad, which I totally borrow for my games.<br /> <br /> Or a Deva or 3rd Circle Soul that exists as a haunted Game, like a Memetic entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There should be an auction house or a market stall (3rd circle demon) that lets you buy and sell anything. Social status, love, attributes and abilities, exp for charms and such, and maybe even more esoterics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T05:34:42-07:00","id":1389938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1389936#post1389936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be an auction house or a market stall (3rd circle demon) that lets you buy and sell anything. Social status, love, attributes and abilities, exp for charms and such, and maybe even more esoterics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Living Goblin Market... Hmmm Maybe its form is a bazaar that appears under bridges. Bridges symbolizing conveyance which is abstractly connected to the idea of exchange. Yes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:21:10-07:00","id":1389951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1389938#post1389938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Living Goblin Market... Hmmm Maybe its form is a bazaar that appears under bridges. Bridges symbolizing conveyance which is abstractly connected to the idea of exchange. Yes...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put in a gambling den, if it wasn't for the fact that such an idea was already taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:29:25-07:00","id":1390077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1389936#post1389936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be an auction house or a market stall (3rd circle demon) that lets you buy and sell anything. Social status, love, attributes and abilities, exp for charms and such, and maybe even more esoterics.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/287087\" target=\"_blank\">Makarios</a> not do it for you?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1389951#post1389951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would put in a gambling den, if it wasn't for the fact that such an idea was already taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the bridge idea. But nothing stops you making it a <i>demonic</i> gambling den in direct competition with Plentimon.<br /> <br /> Heck, I'd make it a demonic gambling den that appears under bridges. Perhaps when someone survives throwing themselves off the bridge to escape their gambling debts it appears in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T18:08:51-07:00","id":1390137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1390077#post1390077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/287087\" target=\"_blank\">Makarios</a> not do it for you?<br /> I like the bridge idea. But nothing stops you making it a <i>demonic</i> gambling den in direct competition with Plentimon.<br /> <br /> Heck, I'd make it a demonic gambling den that appears under bridges. Perhaps when someone survives throwing themselves off the bridge to escape their gambling debts it appears in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Markarios buys dreams and sells artifacts.<br /> <br /> I'm more thinking of a location where anyone can enter, and anyone can buy and sell. It's like one of those farmer markets, only that instead of produce you're selling your own traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:56:55-07:00","id":1390192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1390137#post1390137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Markarios buys dreams and sells artifacts.<br /> <br /> I'm more thinking of a location where anyone can enter, and anyone can buy and sell. It's like one of those farmer markets, only that instead of produce you're selling your own traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Sigereth, but instead of gambling traits you buy and sell them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T23:44:19-07:00","id":1390213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1390137#post1390137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Markarios buys dreams and sells artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makarios buys dreams and sells crystallized sadness and the language of toads. I'm pretty sure he could sell you brewed glory or bottled fame.<br /> <br /> But I take your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T04:16:54-07:00","id":1390250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1390192#post1390192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Sigereth, but instead of gambling traits you buy and sell them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that. It lets you do it with each other. As in, you don't need the demon to do it for you. The demon isn't a person or merchant, its the market place where you can do it literally. Get 2 mortals, bring them to the genius loci, and one will be able to swap his skill in swordsmanship with the other's skill in seduction. A man will be able to trade one good eye so that his father could gain a working eye to see with. And so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T06:25:52-07:00","id":1390273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1390250#post1390250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just that. It lets you do it with each other. As in, you don't need the demon to do it for you. The demon isn't a person or merchant, its the market place where you can do it literally. Get 2 mortals, bring them to the genius loci, and one will be able to swap his skill in swordsmanship with the other's skill in seduction. A man will be able to trade one good eye so that his father could gain a working eye to see with. And so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea.<br /> <br /> Buuuuutttttt....<br /> <br /> When I sell something on eBay, eBay takes a cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T08:24:43-07:00","id":1390294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1384979-the-demon-tree?p=1390273#post1390273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very cool idea.<br /> <br /> Buuuuutttttt....<br /> <br /> When I sell something on eBay, eBay takes a cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>*thinks* <br /> <br /> Maybe a surcharge? Maybe each and every act of transaction and free trade happening within his borders makes the 3rd circle demon extra essence, in terms of magnitude? Or something like a pool of essence it can use for other things? <br /> <br /> And then it can use that stored up essence to 'enhance' a trade, like say, finding a guy with a specific thing you want, or 'boost' a transaction, so it actually leads to an increase in the total wealth. <br /> <br /> And another thing to note. It can do more than just transfer things like attributes and abiliites. It can trade merits. It can also let you trade around health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}